<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
	xmlns:oa="http://www.openapplications.org/oagis/9"
	xmlns="http://www.mimosa.org/ccom4"
	targetNamespace="http://www.mimosa.org/ccom4"
	elementFormDefault="qualified"
	attributeFormDefault="unqualified">

	<xs:import schemaLocation="../../OAGIS/Meta.xsd" namespace="http://www.openapplications.org/oagis/9"/>
	<xs:include schemaLocation="../CCOMQuery.xsd"/>

	<xs:element name="GetBreakdownStructures">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation xml:lang="en">
Returns 0 to N breakdown structures via a ShowBreakdownStructures response.

The difference between this and GetBreakdownStructureConnections is that GetBreakdownStructureConnections also returns all connections, and may not be suitable if only header data (e.g. identifiers, names, metadata) is required.

Allows optional criteria-based filtering, otherwise all breakdown structures will be returned. Criteria in the same BreakdownStructuresCriteria noun are combined with a logical AND while criteria across different BreakdownStructuresCriteria are combined with a logical OR.

If countOnly = true, then the response only contains the number of breakdown structures, not the data. No value is interpreted as countOnly = false.
			</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:complexContent>
				<xs:extension base="oa:BusinessObjectDocumentType">
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element name="DataArea">
							<xs:complexType>
								<xs:sequence>
									<xs:element ref="oa:Get"/>
									<xs:element name="BreakdownStructuresCriteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
										<xs:complexType>
											<xs:sequence>
												<xs:element name="UUID" type="UUIDFilter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
												<xs:element name="ShortName" type="TextFilter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
												<xs:element name="TypeUUID" type="UUIDFilter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
											</xs:sequence>
										</xs:complexType>
									</xs:element>
								</xs:sequence>
							</xs:complexType>
						</xs:element>
					</xs:sequence>
				</xs:extension>
			</xs:complexContent>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>

</xs:schema>
